-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulation 41.6: DIVISION OF BENEFITS.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- When two or more claimants share the remaining weeks of unpaid benefits for the same child or family member
-- and cannot agree how to divide them, the weeks are divided as the three paragraphs say. The claimants are
-- numbered in the order in which they made their claims (1 for the first to make a claim). A division the
-- claimants agree on is theirs, not the regulation's, and so is a division fixed by reg 76.21(2) or 76.42(2)
-- (piece er4: claimants resident in different provinces, one claiming provincial benefits): both are NOTHING here.
-- Out of range: ss 23(4), 23.1(9), 23.2(8), 23.3(6), 152.05(12), 152.06(7), 152.061(8) and 152.062(6) of the Act,
-- which send the claimants here (pieces ei1 and ei5).

§ `Regulation 41.6 -- division of the remaining weeks of benefits`

-- Whole numbers of weeks. Paragraph (a): the weeks equal the claimants, one week each. Paragraph (b): more weeks
-- than claimants, a week to each in turn starting with the first to make a claim until the weeks are exhausted:
-- each claimant gets the whole number of rounds, and the first (weeks MODULO claimants) claimants one more.
-- Paragraph (c): fewer weeks than claimants, a week to each in turn starting with the first until the weeks are
-- exhausted: the first `weeks` claimants get one and the others none.
-- src:740 | 41.6 For the purposes of subsections 23(4), 23.1(9), 23.2(8), 23.3(6), 152.05(12), 152.06(7), 152.061(8) and 152.062(6) of the Act and subject to subsections 76.21(2) and 76.42(2), if the claimants cannot agree on a division of the remaining weeks of unpaid benefits, those weeks shall be divided as follows:
-- src:741 | (a) if the number of weeks of unpaid benefits equals the number of claimants, each claimant will be paid a week of benefits;
-- src:742 | (b) if the number of weeks of unpaid benefits is more than the number of claimants, a week of benefits will be paid to claimants in turn starting with the first claimant to make a claim until all the weeks have been exhausted; or
-- src:743 | (c) if the number of weeks of unpaid benefits is less than the number of claimants, a week of benefits will be paid to claimants in turn starting with the first claimant to make a claim until all the weeks have been exhausted.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 41.6 (src:740-743)
GIVEN `the claimants cannot agree on a division of the remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the division is fixed by subsection 76.21(2) or 76.42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of claimants` IS A NUMBER
      `the place in the order in which the claimants made their claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 41.6 the weeks of benefits paid to the claimant` IS
    IF    NOT (`the claimants cannot agree on a division of the remaining weeks of unpaid benefits`)
       OR `the division is fixed by subsection 76.21(2) or 76.42(2)`
       OR `the number of claimants` AT MOST 0
       OR `the place in the order in which the claimants made their claims` LESS THAN 1
       OR `the place in the order in which the claimants made their claims` GREATER THAN `the number of claimants`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE BRANCH
            -- (a)
            IF `the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` EQUALS `the number of claimants`
            THEN JUST 1
            -- (b)
            IF `the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` GREATER THAN `the number of claimants`
            THEN JUST ((FLOOR (`the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` DIVIDED BY `the number of claimants`))
                       PLUS (IF `the place in the order in which the claimants made their claims` AT MOST (`the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` MODULO `the number of claimants`) THEN 1 ELSE 0))
            -- (c)
            OTHERWISE JUST (IF `the place in the order in which the claimants made their claims` AT MOST `the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- reg 41.1, 41.11, 41.3, 41.4, 41.5 are repealed and sit in er3-sickness-pregnancy.
